Diagram metadata schema:
Every executable mxCell node should support these attributes:

data-logic-id
data-node-type
data-route
data-prompt-id
data-kb-ref
data-entry
data-priority
data-tags
data-state
data-next
data-condition
data-camera-x
data-camera-y
data-camera-zoom

Node types:
- entry
- route
- decision
- prompt
- knowledge
- system
- scene
- action
- terminal

Example node:

<mxCell
  id="node-kb-query"
  value="Ask Knowledgebase"
  vertex="1"
  parent="1"
  data-logic-id="kb.query"
  data-node-type="knowledge"
  data-route="/engine/kb/query"
  data-prompt-id="kb-context-query"
  data-kb-ref="core.engine.routing"
  data-next="node-decision"
  data-camera-x="420"
  data-camera-y="260"
  data-camera-zoom="1.3">
  <mxGeometry x="360" y="220" width="160" height="80" as="geometry"/>
</mxCell>

Implement TypeScript types:

type DiagramNode = {
  id: string
  label: string
  logicId: string
  nodeType: DiagramNodeType
  route?: string
  promptId?: string
  kbRef?: string
  entry?: boolean
  priority?: number
  tags: string[]
  state?: string
  next: string[]
  condition?: string
  camera?: {
    x: number
    y: number
    zoom: number
  }
  geometry: {
    x: number
    y: number
    width: number
    height: number
  }
}

type DiagramEdge = {
  id: string
  source: string
  target: string
  label?: string
  condition?: string
}

type DiagramGraph = {
  nodes: Record<string, DiagramNode>
  edges: DiagramEdge[]
  entryNodeId: string
}

Implement parser:
- Fetch /diagrams/main-engine.drawio
- Parse XML with DOMParser
- Extract mxCell nodes with vertex="1"
- Extract mxCell edges with edge="1"
- Read custom data-* attributes
- Build DiagramGraph
- Resolve entry node by data-entry="true" or first nodeType="entry"

Implement router:
- Maintain currentNodeId
- stepForward()
- stepBack()
- jumpTo(logicIdOrNodeId)
- getAvailableTransitions()
- evaluateCondition(condition, engineContext)
- routeToNode(nodeId)

Engine state:

type EngineState = {
  graph: DiagramGraph | null
  currentNodeId: string | null
  history: string[]
  variables: Record<string, unknown>
  mode: "play" | "godmode" | "replay"
  activeFilters: {
    nodeTypes: string[]
    tags: string[]
    kbRefs: string[]
  }
}

Prompt-in-place system:
- If active node has data-prompt-id, resolve it from promptRegistry
- Combine prompt template with:
  - current node metadata
  - current route
  - current knowledgebase reference
  - engine variables
  - previous node history
- Return a ready-to-send prompt string
- Do not call an external AI API yet; expose prompt text for integration

Prompt registry example:

